# S26 port of testkit's scenarios/reload-cycle. UNLIKE reload-mid-upload
# next door, this one DOES use cache_turbo's own probe: proving that
# cache_turbo_probe survives a live SIGHUP series is the entire point of this
# scenario. Before S26 (CTPROBE-STATIC-ZONE-NO-RELOAD,
# memory/labs/nginx-cache-turbo-module/issues.md) the probe zone pointer was
# a process-lifetime static that the directive handler's duplicate guard
# rejected on the SECOND config parse -- every reload here would have died
# at `nginx -t`-equivalent with "cache_turbo_probe is duplicate" before a
# single HUP was even sent. This scenario is the reload-spanning proof that
# fix works: it reads cache_turbo's own zone counters (hits/misses/lookups)
# across a live reload series, which only compiles into a working request at
# all once the second-parse rejection is gone.
PROBER_PROBE='cache_turbo_probe ct;'
